WEBVTT

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:03.160
If I throw it at full force...

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:06.190
...it's like this!

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:14.410
All right, nice!

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:16.960
Even at full force, I can control the ball.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:21.270
All right. Now I've gotta work 
on fine tuning my aim...

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.290
Look here. Why do I have to go 
that far just to catch for you?

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:28.300
I'm not even a catcher.

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:33.340
Then, you should become a catcher!

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:34.330
Huh?

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:37.660
That's it! That's a great idea, Daigo-kun.

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:39.430
You should make becoming
 a catcher your goal!

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:41.860
You learn how to catch my pitches,

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:45.190
and then, we can challenge 
 the Urabe and Andy battery!

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:49.800
M-Me? A catcher?!

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:21.280
Oh, no...

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:22.870
Oh, no, no, no, no, no...

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:28.010
Look at you, brown-nosing just because
you want your very own bullpen catcher.

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:29.420
Commence 
Special Training!

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:29.870
I see through you!

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:31.660
I see right through you!

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:36.760
With my weak arm, being a catcher is 
just as impossible as being a pitcher!

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:38.510
There's so much to do, too.

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:41.140
In some ways, it's the hardest position!

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:43.020
And even if you want me in that role,

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:45.890
there's no way Coach is gonna 
use me if I'm worse than Andy.

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:47.880
One month...

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:52.520
No. Even <i>years </i>of practice wouldn't be 
enough to make me a proper catcher!

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:07.490
H-Hey, why are you leaving, Hikaru?

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:10.720
<i>Is he mad?</i>

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:13.330
You can practice in our yard.

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:16.000
Don't you want to use 
that board over there?

00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:21.090
I shouldn't have made a ludicrous request
 when I know nothing about baseball.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:26.100
I was just thinking how fun it would be 
to go out on the field together,

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:30.420
with you catching my pitches in a game.

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:35.020
But if it's not realistic, then that's that.

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:38.880
Well, I'll just go practice by myself.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:39.620
Later.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:51.860
Hey, Daigo, was that Satou-kun?
The kid in uniform?

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:53.840
He's pretty cute!

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:59.570
Hey! Anybody home?

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:02.050
Hey, what's wrong with you?

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:14.370
You won't know that until you give it a go.

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:19.530
You really need to just 
stop caring about that.

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:23.300
There's nothing wrong with 
a little embarrassment.

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:28.910
But it's definitely wrong to let potential 
embarrassment get in the way of curiosity.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:33.120
I shouldn't have made a ludicrous request
 when I know nothing about baseball.

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:38.130
I was just thinking how fun it would be 
to go out on the field together,

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:42.330
with you catching my pitches in a game.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.630
Hey, Sis.

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:49.510
Huh?

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:52.140
You ever play as a catcher?

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:54.430
What a random question.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:57.230
No, I haven't. Why do you ask?

00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:02.390
If I said I wanted to be a catcher, 
everyone would laugh it off, right?

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:07.190
I wouldn't laugh.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:08.770
What?

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:09.900
Liar!

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:12.580
You don't honestly think I could 
do it with my weak arm, do you?

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:14.690
I'm not lying.

00:05:14.690 --> 00:05:17.190
When I was playing for the Dolphins,

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:19.670
they didn't have anyone 
who wanted to play catcher,

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:22.590
so they made this one kid with 
seriously bad motor skills do it.

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:26.700
The catcher for my current middle 
school team is just some average joe.

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:33.920
Yeah, but I bet they can 
at least throw to second.

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:37.600
They match up people with the 
positions that fit them best.

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:43.790
Look, you're over-thinking it.

00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:49.870
It's understandable, since you grew up
surrounded by Dad's games and all that info.

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:54.330
But in junior baseball,
just wanting it makes you suitable.

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:57.550
Throwing a ball to second?

00:05:57.550 --> 00:06:01.000
Unless you're playing professionally, 
that's not so important.

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:05.930
The guy catching for us right now 
doesn't have a particularly strong arm,

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:07.630
but he knows a lot, and he's observant.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:11.590
That's enough for us to 
trust him with the mask.

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:17.390
How to line up the defense, 
based on the game situation...

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:19.090
How to position the outfielders...

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:22.180
Strategies to employ 
against the current batter...

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:24.860
You may not have the experience,

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:28.900
but in terms of knowledge, you're more 
than a match for your teammates, right?

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:41.740
I mean, personality-wise,

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:44.040
catcher might actually suit you.

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:48.300
Catcher...

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:58.190
<i>Guess I'll have to help him.</i>

00:06:58.190 --> 00:07:01.230
<i>I doubt I'll get to play in any games,</i>

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:05.110
<i>but if it helps out Hikaru, 
I'll be his practice buddy!</i>

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:11.700
So this is where he lives.

00:07:14.110 --> 00:07:18.250
Looks pretty average for someone 
whose dad used to play in the majors.

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:26.870
There he is!

00:07:26.870 --> 00:07:28.590
Good work, Hikaru!

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:31.760
Hey, Hikaru!

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:33.300
Daigo-kun?

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:37.440
I've been thinking about 
what you said before...

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:39.940
Y'know, that stuff about being a catcher...

00:07:39.940 --> 00:07:41.980
Oh, it's fine.

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:44.330
I found someone else to practice with me.

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:44.980
Huh?

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:50.370
What?!

00:07:50.370 --> 00:07:52.650
S-S-S-Sakura?!

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:56.380
She told me a while back that
she had a hankering to play catch,

00:07:56.380 --> 00:07:59.400
so when I asked her out of the blue, 
she jumped at the chance.

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:01.580
But... a girl?

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:12.600
Well, as you can see, she's really good.

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:14.040
Amazing, isn't it?

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:17.950
She said she might even join the Dolphins.

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:22.020
You can't be serious!

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:24.440
How can she be a catcher?

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:28.400
Why is a girl calmly catching 
your brutal fastballs?

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:31.710
Mutsuko-chan told me her older 
brother used to play baseball.

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:35.910
She was his catching practice 
partner, so she got really good.

00:08:36.630 --> 00:08:39.410
Shigeno-kun, you don't want 
to play catcher, right?

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:43.910
That's why I thought I'd 
practice with Hikaru-kun.

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:47.340
I-I never said I didn't want to...

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:50.170
Well, I guess I <i>did </i>say I didn't, but...

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:52.790
I came over because I changed my mind.

00:08:52.790 --> 00:08:56.480
I figured, as we'd come this far, 
I might as well catch for Hikaru.

00:08:57.950 --> 00:08:59.410
Oh.

00:08:59.410 --> 00:09:01.520
I guess that means you don't need me.

00:09:01.790 --> 00:09:05.960
Too bad. I was so happy I finally 
got to play baseball again.

00:09:07.090 --> 00:09:07.980
But...

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:11.730
Can I really trust you, Daigo-kun?

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:12.720
What?

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:18.060
I don't really feel like you want this.

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:22.240
You still seem unmotivated, 
like you don't have any stake in it.

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:27.500
Daigo-kun, it sounds like you're only in it 
for my sake and that you have no choice.

00:09:29.010 --> 00:09:33.160
Not to mention, saying that you 
"might as well catch for me"?

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:35.680
Why are you talking down to me?

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:38.760
You can't catch my fastballs, can you?

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:44.910
I guess suggesting you try a position 
you'd find difficult was my mistake.

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:50.400
It's fine. You don't have to 
force yourself to be here.

00:09:50.850 --> 00:09:53.440
I found Mutsuko-chan to practice with me.

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:01.330
Fine, whatever!

00:10:03.210 --> 00:10:04.980
He's gone off in a huff.

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:06.760
Are you okay with that?

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:08.090
It's fine.

00:10:08.090 --> 00:10:09.560
I made him mad on purpose.

00:10:11.190 --> 00:10:15.070
But if that's all it takes to make him quit,
he's better off not bothering.

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:32.560
Andou's Sporting Goods

00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:44.980
Are you looking for a mitt?

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:48.170
That makes you a catcher, right?

00:10:48.170 --> 00:10:49.790
What team do you play for?

00:10:52.180 --> 00:10:55.800
Dad, I told you not to talk 
to customers like that!

00:10:56.010 --> 00:10:58.820
And don't come out in the 
store in your innerwear!

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:01.640
What? What was that?

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:07.340
Mom, I want to go online for a bit. 
Can I borrow your tablet?

00:11:08.070 --> 00:11:10.170
Daigo's using it at the moment.

00:11:10.170 --> 00:11:11.020
Huh?

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:15.160
Oh, and listen to this! He's asked 
for a catcher's mitt for his birthday,

00:11:15.160 --> 00:11:18.530
even though it's months away!

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:21.530
What? Really? He's really 
buying into this idea of his!

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:24.490
<i>Damn...</i>

00:11:25.050 --> 00:11:27.810
<i>I thought he was actually a decent guy.</i>

00:11:29.030 --> 00:11:31.120
<i>But as soon as he found 
someone else to practice with,</i>

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:33.260
<i>he dropped me, just like that.</i>

00:11:34.990 --> 00:11:38.050
You can't catch my fastballs, can you?

00:11:42.440 --> 00:11:44.570
<i>How dare he mock me like that...</i>

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:47.900
<i>I'll catch his pitches 
and make it look easy!</i>

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:51.080
<i>I'll show him!</i>

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:58.360
Moving on to question one on the next page...

00:11:58.670 --> 00:12:02.860
Let's use the previous example 
as a guide for how to solve it.

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:14.750
I'm home!

00:12:14.970 --> 00:12:17.290
Mom, did you buy that mitt I wanted?

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:18.800
Of course!

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:24.300
Let's get down to business!

00:12:25.520 --> 00:12:26.540
Excuse me?

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:29.710
What's all this?

00:12:29.710 --> 00:12:31.920
You got me a full set of gear!

00:12:31.920 --> 00:12:34.430
I feel so loved.

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:36.420
And you've bought other stuff, too...

00:12:36.420 --> 00:12:38.350
Of course not.

00:12:39.120 --> 00:12:39.690
Then, how?

00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:43.900
I've known Andou-san over at the 
sporting goods store for a long time.

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:45.410
What's that?

00:12:45.690 --> 00:12:48.790
Goro-kun's son said he 
wanted to be a catcher?

00:12:48.790 --> 00:12:49.280
Yes!

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:51.120
Wait a second...

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:55.870
That reminds me. Yesterday, we had a boy 
in the store looking longingly at a mitt.

00:12:56.800 --> 00:12:58.620
That must've been Daigo!

00:12:58.620 --> 00:12:59.790
Oh, really?

00:12:59.790 --> 00:13:00.940
Well, in that case...

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:05.590
It's used, but still perfectly good.

00:13:05.820 --> 00:13:07.190
Take it with you—

00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:11.180
That old man

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:14.850
was our coach back when your pop and I
played for the Dolphins together.

00:13:14.850 --> 00:13:16.100
Really?

00:13:16.100 --> 00:13:20.610
He was more than happy to give me the gear 
when he heard Shigeno Jr. wanted to catch.

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:21.860
Huh.

00:13:22.270 --> 00:13:24.910
Well, that's all fine...

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:29.150
...but what's with your getup?

00:13:29.150 --> 00:13:31.830
Isn't that obvious?

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:35.550
I figure, now my beloved son is 
finally truly interested in baseball,

00:13:35.550 --> 00:13:38.670
it's time for this "master coach"
 to step up her game!

00:13:40.280 --> 00:13:41.670
Don't underestimate me.

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:43.470
Believe it or not,

00:13:43.470 --> 00:13:46.550
I have over ten years' experience 
playing baseball and softball.

00:13:46.900 --> 00:13:49.550
I even played catcher for your father.

00:13:50.920 --> 00:13:53.170
All right, we're going 
to start with the basics!

00:13:53.170 --> 00:13:56.810
What? I only need to 
practice catching fastballs.

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:03.520
We'll start with your posture.

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:07.240
Keep your body steady, make 
a loose fist with your right hand,

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:09.490
and put it behind your thighs or your back.

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:12.860
Like this?

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:17.650
Don't close your eyes.

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:19.100
Keep your eye on the ball.

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:26.500
One more!

00:14:27.830 --> 00:14:28.930
Whoa!

00:14:36.240 --> 00:14:37.680
Move your feet!

00:14:37.960 --> 00:14:40.360
Learn how to use the mitt already.

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:43.450
Oh, you already started.

00:14:44.260 --> 00:14:46.430
Y-You're here, too, Sis?

00:14:50.440 --> 00:14:52.530
Lean your upper body forward.

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:54.780
Otherwise, the ball will 
be deflected behind you.

00:14:55.190 --> 00:14:58.120
Even if you can't catch it,
make sure the ball falls in front of you.

00:15:04.590 --> 00:15:05.910
Take off the mask!

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:10.920
Make sure your front foot is pointing in
the direction you're thrower the ball.

00:15:16.970 --> 00:15:17.560
Ow!

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:27.580
I can't! Timeout.

00:15:27.580 --> 00:15:29.150
I need a break.

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:31.870
What? Pull yourself together.

00:15:31.870 --> 00:15:34.070
You've only been at it for an hour.

00:15:34.570 --> 00:15:37.160
Kids these days are unbelievable.

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:39.490
In my day, we were a lot tougher.

00:15:39.490 --> 00:15:40.720
Really?

00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:41.790
Yup.

00:15:42.050 --> 00:15:45.500
Well, let's practice 
catching some fastballs.

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:48.580
Finally! That's it!

00:15:48.580 --> 00:15:50.620
That's what I've been wanting to do all along!

00:15:50.620 --> 00:15:52.880
Want me to pitch, then?

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:54.800
Tut, tut, tut.

00:15:57.000 --> 00:16:00.310
Don't take me lightly just 
because I'm nearly forty.

00:16:00.580 --> 00:16:03.840
I'm built quite unlike most women my age!

00:16:08.870 --> 00:16:09.900
Here I go.

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:23.040
M-Mom!

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:24.210
Mama!

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:28.210
This is a prime example of what 
we call "the frozen shoulder."

00:16:28.770 --> 00:16:33.340
It'll heal by itself, but until then, 
baseball and anything like it are out.

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:35.700
"Quite unlike most women my age," my foot.

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:49.470
Daigo!

00:16:50.850 --> 00:16:54.160
I could help you with simple drills.

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:55.910
Must be boring doing that all by yourself.

00:16:57.880 --> 00:17:01.040
The doctor told you to rest up for a while.

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:03.520
Old women shouldn't 
overstretch themselves.

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:08.970
Anyway, do you know anyone 
who can throw fastballs?

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:12.550
Sis has team practice, so I can't ask her.

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:17.840
If I can't practice catching fastballs, 
all of this is pointless.

00:17:18.740 --> 00:17:21.770
Of course, I need someone who won't
 break down after the first throw.

00:17:24.660 --> 00:17:29.860
Well, I do know a lot of old players from 
way back when, but they all have jobs.

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:34.150
Oh, why not ask your manager, 
Tashiro, or Coach Fujii?

00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:36.100
I can't do that.

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:39.910
Me becoming a catcher this late 
doesn't fit the team vision.

00:17:40.520 --> 00:17:42.740
I'm just doing this on my own.

00:17:44.390 --> 00:17:46.220
I guess there's nothing for it.

00:17:46.220 --> 00:17:49.040
Well, I am sort of responsible for this...

00:17:49.470 --> 00:17:51.040
Here. Pocket money.

00:17:51.260 --> 00:17:52.000
Huh?

00:17:52.420 --> 00:17:54.670
Why not go practice at a batting center?

00:17:55.080 --> 00:17:57.680
You can catch fastballs there.

00:17:59.710 --> 00:18:01.610
I never thought of that!

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:06.430
Mifune Batting Center

00:18:04.900 --> 00:18:06.430
Next one is the last!

00:18:10.770 --> 00:18:12.730
Home Run

00:18:12.730 --> 00:18:15.120
Aw, man, so close!

00:18:21.340 --> 00:18:24.310
I've heard tales of pros doing 
things like that in the past,

00:18:24.310 --> 00:18:27.080
but this is the first time I've 
actually seen someone catching here.

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:31.330
<i>Ack! They saw me!</i>

00:18:32.050 --> 00:18:35.130
<i>Stop gawking! If you're done, go home!</i>

00:18:40.520 --> 00:18:43.230
<i>How embarrassing. 
That was all because they were...</i>

00:18:44.190 --> 00:18:45.750
They're gone?!

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:53.230
This mitt is still stiff 
and not easy to use yet.

00:18:53.880 --> 00:18:58.220
The mitt I used the other day that belonged 
to Hikaru's father was really easy to use.

00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:11.970
Guess I'm comfortable with 110 kmph now.

00:19:12.740 --> 00:19:14.790
I'm done with my warm up.

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:17.010
Fast balls

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:17.010
For both 
batting 
positions

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:17.010
Right-handed 
pitcher

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:18.700
Now, for the real deal.

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:21.430
High

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:21.430
Low

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:23.840
Oh, I need my mask!

00:19:36.580 --> 00:19:38.170
That <i>is</i> fast.

00:19:38.170 --> 00:19:39.900
The ball's pushing my mitt away.

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:51.510
Ow!

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:54.730
It hurts because you're not 
catching them with the pocket.

00:19:57.790 --> 00:20:00.380
<i>What the hell? Another heckler's shown up?</i>

00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:03.930
It's dangerous to look away.

00:20:10.180 --> 00:20:11.940
<i>I finally caught it.</i>

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:14.190
Your mitt isn't still enough.

00:20:14.710 --> 00:20:17.190
The pitcher won't be comfortable with that.

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:18.500
<i>How annoying.</i>

00:20:18.500 --> 00:20:20.820
<i>Does this old fart think 
he's a baseball coach now?</i>

00:20:20.820 --> 00:20:22.200
<i>Go away!</i>

00:20:22.990 --> 00:20:26.220
You're afraid, so you're only 
using your hand to catch.

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:31.290
Try positioning your lower body properly
so you can catch it in front of you.

00:20:36.800 --> 00:20:37.490
See?

00:20:37.490 --> 00:20:39.180
Since you're only moving your hand,

00:20:39.860 --> 00:20:44.340
your mitt obstructs your vision,
and you can't keep your eye on the ball.

00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:49.220
Your biggest problem is the way
you're holding the mitt. It's too stiff.

00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:54.080
The pitcher needs you to hold up the mitt,
but once he makes his pitch,

00:20:54.080 --> 00:20:57.070
lowering it before you catch
can help you relax and loosen up.

00:20:57.870 --> 00:20:59.800
The ball is fast,

00:20:59.800 --> 00:21:03.110
but essentially, it's the 
same as playing catch.

00:21:03.580 --> 00:21:05.750
<i>The same as playing catch?</i>

00:21:18.280 --> 00:21:19.060
<i>Huh?</i>

00:21:20.320 --> 00:21:21.190
<i>Why?</i>

00:21:21.190 --> 00:21:23.020
<i>That was so easy to catch.</i>

00:21:25.560 --> 00:21:26.720
What?!

00:21:29.200 --> 00:21:31.020
E-Excuse me, sir!

00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:37.980
U-Uh... I don't know where 
you used to play baseball,

00:21:38.480 --> 00:21:40.570
but that was really helpful!

00:21:40.800 --> 00:21:42.330
Thank you very much!

00:21:43.190 --> 00:21:45.780
Oh, that's great to hear.

00:21:49.180 --> 00:21:53.540
Looks like playing baseball till I made it 
to the majors wasn't totally in vain.

00:21:58.040 --> 00:22:01.040
S-S-Satou T-T-Toshiya?!

00:22:01.660 --> 00:22:04.410
I don't have any time today because of work,

00:22:04.410 --> 00:22:05.920
but I'll be back tomorrow.

00:22:05.920 --> 00:22:06.740
Huh?

00:22:06.740 --> 00:22:08.970
Don't worry about it.

00:22:09.510 --> 00:22:13.380
It was your pop who asked me to coach you.

00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:18.620
What?!

00:22:18.620 --> 00:22:20.440
"C-Coach"?!

00:22:20.440 --> 00:22:21.960
Pop's behind this?!

00:22:22.320 --> 00:22:26.320
What... What is even going on here?

00:24:00.710 --> 00:24:01.580
No way!

00:24:01.780 --> 00:24:04.430
<i>The</i> Satou Toshiya is my coach?

00:24:04.430 --> 00:24:06.460
And it was Pop who asked him to coach me?

00:24:07.090 --> 00:24:10.160
I might actually become 
an amazing catcher now!

00:24:10.710 --> 00:24:15.340
But wait... why isn't Hikaru 
learning from his father?

00:24:15.710 --> 00:24:18.010
Hikaru's being weird.

00:24:18.010 --> 00:24:25.020
Catch

00:24:19.090 --> 00:24:21.300
Next time: Catch.

00:24:21.300 --> 00:24:23.420
Run to the stage of your dreams!
